  "flag_reading": [
    "A flag is kind:field:cause. Fields are the finding schema's names: cvss_base, composite_score, severity_band, remediation_sla, risk_disposition, review_date, reachability, cvss_vector.",
    "Step reading of D9's causes: a changed cvss_base is 'vector', a changed composite_score is 'arithmetic', a changed severity_band is 'band-mapping' (or 'rounding' for a tie), and a changed remediation_sla, risk_disposition or review_date is 'follows-band'. A change that the asset tags alone explain takes 'retagged' and the cause 'asset-tags' on every field it moves (ruling A).",
    "basis 'pinned': the flag string appears in ADR-050, the spec or the contracts. 'derived': composed from that grammar by the reading above. 'optional': the renderer may add it or not, and a test must accept both.",
    "A flag that the renderer adds and that is not listed is a defect of one side: the list is complete for the cases here."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Six carried legacy rows scored before any tags applied, so each tag that the chosen source applies shows as a retag: 'elevated-by-pii' (the band rises) and 'elevated-by-secrets' (the band holds) move; 'pii-is-no-op' and 'secrets-is-no-op' carry bits their vectors already have; the two findings on tool-server-1 move only if a source gives that component the auth tag.",
    "The source is chosen once per run and never mixed: a run that scores one component from the block and another from the architecture has failed this case. The warning is recorded in the stage record, and the run never stops for it (FR-N16.2, S-13).",
    "The block's auth tag on tool-server-1 cannot be checked and is applied: that is what 'unverified' means. The command's own architecture path is absent, so there is nothing to recompute from."
  ],
